{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C++ header file", "description": "This file defines the 'Configuration' class in the 'prplmesh::hostapd' namespace. It provides an interface for managing hostapd configuration files, including loading, storing, and modifying configuration parameters for Virtual Access Points (VAPs). The class supports operations like retrieving and setting key-value pairs in the configuration head and VAP sections, disabling VAPs, and iterating over VAPs with predicates. The file also declares related template functions for iteration and an output operator for debugging.", "external_files": ["<iostream>", "<map>", "<set>", "<string>", "<vector>"], "external_methods": [], "published": ["Configuration", "operator bool()", "update_required()", "load", "store", "set_create_head_value", "get_head_value", "get_vap_by_bssid", "set_create_vap_value", "set_create_value", "get_vap_value", "disable_vap", "for_all_ap_vaps", "operator<<", "get_last_message"], "classes": [{"name": "Configuration", "description": "Manages parsing, editing, and saving hostapd configuration files, focusing on VAP settings and key-value pairs."}], "methods": [{"name": "operator bool()", "description": "Returns true if the configuration is non-empty and valid, false otherwise."}, {"name": "update_required()", "description": "Indicates whether the current configuration has pending updates that need to be saved."}, {"name": "bool load(const StringIndications...vap_indications)", "description": "Loads configuration data from the associated file, using specified vap indications.", "scope": "prplmesh::hostapd::Configuration", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "store", "description": "Stores the current in-memory configuration back to the file."}, {"name": "set_create_head_value", "description": "Sets a key-value pair in the head section of the configuration, either replacing or creating it."}, {"name": "get_head_value", "description": "Retrieves the value associated with a given key from t